  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The text follows the written history and compiled science of an intriguing building that was constructed as a monument to mythology and to house the most advanced in scientific instruments. The tower has had many functions both mechanical and spiritual, and much of it has been "explained" by scholars from antiquity up to the present time. Yet the Tower of the Winds was and still is a mystery to those involved in the complex study of it." -- Foolscap Press website, accessed 4/23/2012.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="504" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Includes bibliographical references.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="505" ind1="0" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">1. Athens -- 2. Plato's pavilion -- 3. The winds -- 4. The test of 1844 -- 5. A mainspring of technology -- 6. The sun, the winds &amp; time.</subfield>
  </datafield>
